The ACL rule on dswa1/dswa2 (`DROP FORWARD 10.1.0.0/24→10.3.0.0/24 on br0.10`) was flagged by infra_sweep but is NOT causing the reported outage — pc1→pc3 pings at 0% loss confirm that cross-zone routing does not traverse that interface, making the rule a dead-code artifact of "last night's change," not the active fault.

